hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1003","Yunus bin Abdul-Ala and Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, they said: Ibn Wahb told us, Jarir bin Hazim told me, On the authority of Suleiman ibn Mahran, on the authority of Abu Dhabyan, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: Ali ibn Abi Talib passed by an insane woman from the tribe of so-and-so. She had committed adultery. He ordered Omar stoned her, so Ali brought her back and said to Omar: O Commander of the Faithful, will you stone this woman? He said: Yes. He said: Do you not remember that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The pen was lifted from three people: from the insane person who lost his mind, And on behalf of a sleeping person until he wakes up, and on behalf of a boy until he has a wet dream.” He said, “You have spoken the truth,” so he let go of her."
